  {
   "key": "what_exists",
   "title": "What exists already",
   "text": "Several patient groups around the world focus on MPS IIIA, including the Cure Sanfilippo Foundation in the United States and the MPS Society in the United Kingdom [E80ea2ad, E10d7132]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, there is a trial testing a gene therapy called UX111 for MPS IIIA, listed as recruiting with sites in the United States, Australia, and Spain [Eebc4df2, Eb3c0db6, E4164417, E5dbae4a]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, there is also a Phase 1 trial of a treatment called GC1130A for MPS IIIA, with sites in South Korea and the United States [E061da6f, Efebcb7f, E16fc2e1]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, a disease monitoring program for MPS IIIA run by Ultragenyx Pharmaceutical Inc is listed as not yet recruiting [E9c5e5c2, Eebc59b6]. According to NIH RePORTER, a research grant called 'Characterizing and treating peripheral nervous system dysfunction in Sanfilippo Syndrome,' funded by NIH NINDS, studies MPS IIIA [E53b781a, E3577148].",
